# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The uploaded images directory — nothing executes here, under any circumstances
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Defence in depth, not the first line of defence. Uploads are already guarded by three
# things: the extension is derived from the file's content through mime_content_type rather
# than from its name, the stored name is entirely random, and X-Content-Type-Options:
# nosniff stops the browser guessing the type.
#
# But all three live in the application layer or the browser. This file tells the server
# itself: whatever reaches here does not run. The case it covers is a misconfiguration
# somewhere else — an inherited AddHandler, or a PHP handler bound to an unexpected
# extension — and those are cases invisible to anyone reading the upload code.

# ── Prevent PHP execution in all its forms ───────────────────
<FilesMatch "\.(?i:php|php[0-9]?|phtml|phps|phar|inc|hh)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# The PHP handlers are removed explicitly: Require all denied blocks the request, and this
# blocks execution even if the file is reached through an include from somewhere else.
<IfModule mod_php.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php7.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php8.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>

RemoveHandler .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar
RemoveType .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar

# ── And no CGI, and no SSI ───────────────────────────────────
Options -ExecCGI -Includes -Indexes
